body:
TermAl handoff and continuity rules (Termal::Fable2). Rev 8 condenses revs 1–7, 2026-11-13 at about 03:57Z; the history is in those revisions. This MIRRORS the shared Engram rules-push-handoff-2026-11-13 (rev 3+), which governs where the two differ.
GREG'S WORDS (via Asistant): #1500 „reguly przekazywania dalej sesji musza byc precyzyjne”; #1507 „prace muszą iść cały czas. Bez watcher'a czy mojego 'status'”; #1513 „wylaczmy watcher. Jak przestanie pracowac to poprawimy.”
CAUSE OF THE 03:30Z "nobody works": the FULL train was running on runners the session list doesn't show. The real gaps were unassigned coders (the coordinator's fault), one lost placement request, and display-name sends that didn't wake (w-ee0454f76b19).
RULES:
1. Who to whom. Coordinator → coder: assignment. Coder → Opus2: READY or placement. Opus2 → coder: GO or result. Coder → coordinator: done or blocked. Greg is reached only through Asistant.
2. Queue depth 2. Every coder holds a current item plus a named NEXT. While the current item waits, it does NEXT's read-only plan, and claims NEXT once the current item is in review or gate. On finishing, the coordinator tops the queue back up in the same turn.
3. Push. Whoever finishes a step wakes the next owner directly, in the same turn. Resource owners (Opus2, the Merger) send the next GO on each END. NEXT names the item plus its dependency id: run, commit, root generation or fence.
4. Delivery. Use the exact native id (session-N, or host:UUID::session-N), never a display name. A receipt is not delivery. Check the exact messageId's status. Retry only with the identical message, key and route. If a message went down a wrong route, send the recipient a native pointer (mailbox and id) without its content.
5. Non-pickup. The 20/40-minute thresholds are reference values, checked only on a wake, and only for COORDINATION requests, never for a healthy run. Before any ping or takeover, check the message status, the recipient's ACK, the run's terminal state and the claim/fence. Take over only through an Engram offer/accept plus a native wake, or a recovery claim after a lapse. "Idle" in the list proves nothing.
6. NO watcher of any kind. The cron was deleted at 03:52Z. TermAl's internal handoff-ledger 2 s poll is left as it is, and nothing relies on it as a watcher. Allowed: a ONE-SHOT wake for a fixed-time named event, for example the 09:00Z rollback-hold review, or the act-holds start+15 deadline set only after Greg's „zaczynam” (rules-greg-act-holds-2026-11-12 rev 3; both coordinators concur, #7760/#7762; Greg told so he can overrule).
7. Event coverage is only: resume_after_test_runs, delegation fan-in, the native mailbox wake, and an Engram offer/accept plus a native wake.
KNOWN RECOVERY GAPS, fixed when they bite, never with timers:
- w-ee0454f76b19: display-name sends;
- w-80e0cb2002da and w-eb21662dce0a: stop, pause or a failed turn holds the queue;
- w-39913168aff4: a turn dies after accepting a wake;
- w-acb69d529a71: an ACK continuation is not rebuilt;
- w-e328556b6a60: offline-peer redrive;
- no route to the recovery owner, a stated gap.
QUEUES SET at 03:48Z:
